# DECLARED pre-open GEX publisher, per environment. THE source of truth for which
# publisher owns the pre-open (before-09:30) gamma surface.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (incident 2026-08-24): two publishers can serve pre-open GEX and
# they are mutually exclusive by construction -- IbkrPreOpenService is built only when
# IBKR_GEX_CONSUME_ENABLED=true and the service BOOT-REFUSES when the legacy
# PREOPEN_GEX_ENABLED publisher is also on. Because BOTH settings are individually valid,
# a render that silently selects the other publisher is not a syntax error anywhere: it
# deploys cleanly and pre-market GEX simply stops appearing.
#
# That is exactly what happened. Dev ran the IBKR window from 08-21. Commit 075a87d2 had
# flipped the COMMITTED dev intent to the Databento in-service scheduler four days
# earlier but was never deployed, so main and the live cluster disagreed with nothing to
# surface it. A routine config-only `service-deploy databento-gex dev` then applied that
# stale intent and switched the working live-API publisher OFF mid pre-market.
#
# scripts/ci/validate-preopen-single-publisher.sh asserts every rendered overlay matches
# the value declared here. Changing the publisher therefore REQUIRES editing this file in
# the same PR -- an explicit, reviewed act that shows up in the diff -- and can never
# again be a side effect of an unrelated patch, a merge order, or a stale branch.
#
# Values: IBKR      = IBKR live-API pre-open window
#                     (IBKR_GEX_CONSUME_ENABLED=true, IBKR_GEX_PUBLISH_ENABLED=true,
#                      PREOPEN_GEX_ENABLED=false)
#         DATABENTO = legacy in-service scheduler
#                     (PREOPEN_GEX_ENABLED=true, both IBKR_GEX_* false)
#         NONE      = pre-open GEX deliberately off for this environment
#
# dev and production are deliberately kept on the SAME publisher (rule.md: dev = prod).
PREOPEN_PUBLISHER_DEV=IBKR
PREOPEN_PUBLISHER_PRODUCTION=IBKR
PREOPEN_PUBLISHER_EXPERIMENT=NONE
